{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: correct agent-guard loop timestamps so each finding describes the run that produced its counters.\n\nAt current main c9bdbd32792008e942727248c2cf9ecb30f7d2d8, a successful action at t1 followed by failures at t2, t3 and t4 produces a repeated-failure finding with count 3, but first_observed_unix_nano=t1. The documented run begins at t2. The [fold](tailapps/agent-guard/folds/guard.jsonata@c9bdbd32792008e942727248c2cf9ecb30f7d2d8:16) reuses session-first activity for every loop kind at line 58; the [README](tailapps/agent-guard/README.md@c9bdbd32792008e942727248c2cf9ecb30f7d2d8:115) promises the aggregated run. The [existing timestamp test](tailapps/embed_test.go@c9bdbd32792008e942727248c2cf9ecb30f7d2d8:339) repeats one timestamp and cannot distinguish these cases. See the [actual failing probe output](loop-time-probe.log) and [isolated probe source](loop-time-probe_test.go).\n\nThis is a newly confirmed residual correctness defect from the closed timestamp delivery, not a reason to reopen its completed implementation/review records. The original #2200 asked for first/last times where a finding aggregates a run. Its approved composition d53bfc20 and merge a838bfc9 are both ancestors of current main.\n\nQueue this after the full I7 Stage 1 outcome, Kiro #4055 and install guidance #4129, before URL companions/documentation #4087. Keep those commitments live. Reconcile current published bases when starting. The three bases here are live; two carry ordinary inherited staleness. I checked that the relevant fold, schema, test and README blobs are identical between these publication heads and current main, and confirm this outcome, performer, destination and authority remain unchanged. This is no request to clear or refile ordinary staleness.","body":{"conditions":"Deliver a small correction on request/guard-loop-run-times in a new worktree from then-current main. Preserve finding IDs, counter thresholds, finding precedence, per-session latest-row behavior, policy/coverage semantics and confinement. Define and implement first/last observed timestamps for the particular repeated-failure, repeated-action and bounded-no-progress run represented by each row; do not substitute the session start or silently relabel the promised run as a session interval. Handle resets, intervening unknown success/progress telemetry and subsequent runs consistently with existing counters. Missing evidence stays unknown. Prefer the least additional retained state sufficient for honest timestamps; no new tables, event history store, wall-clock monitor or runtime/evaluator change is needed. Explain any unavoidable writable-shape/activation-digest change and its reset/data-loss consequence in the guard README and artifact; do not activate or reset any real resident.\n\nValidation must use distinct source nano-string timestamps: unrelated earlier successful activity followed by three failures; a reset followed by a second qualifying run; changed action fingerprints; observed no-progress runs and absent/unknown progress controls. Exercise actual loaded normalizer/fold and persistent row feedback where relevant. Prove the original fold fails the distinguishing first-time assertion and the correction passes; preserve triggering last time, counters, stable finding IDs and first/last coverage bounds. Include exact affected revision fixtures only where changed, targeted package checks plus required repository gates, and avoid unrelated test expansion. The attached probe is an isolated actual execution at the stated head, not a committed project test or a fix.\n\nPublish exact-path artifacts with tests and actual activation consequences. Request fresh independent Checker review of the exact head and complete artifact set, including architecture/security/simplification conclusions and current basis reconciliation. Ratify that approval, perform the sealed merge to main with exact-path succession, push source and workroom refs, verify main